# Vendored third-party assets are stored byte-for-byte as published. Line-ending
# conversion would change their bytes between platforms, which matters here
# because the Mini App's cache-busting fingerprint is a hash of the file: the
# same release would get a different ?v= on Windows and on Linux, and the phone
# would be told to re-fetch a library that had not changed.
miniapp/vendor/** -text
